Subject: Stop visibly on unsupported kernel paths instead of faking success

An unbridged kernel ordinal, a thread whose start routine is not in the dispatch table, running
out of thread stacks, a wait on a dispatcher object the runtime does not model, HalReturnToFirmware
and KeBugCheck(Ex) now stop the process with a distinct exit code and a log line
(src/fci_manual.c) instead of returning success or exiting 0. A bug check never returns: the game
used to run on past its own fatal error and crash later somewhere unrelated.

---
